# SO-101 run sheet. E215: A gripper call that says nothing.
# Serve e215/lazy_pilot.py in a second terminal, then run this from the root of this checkout, against the arm registered as arm-01:
#   quackd run docs/examples/lerobot/e215/hold-on.duck --robot arm-01 --by-hand --llm local:lazy --base-url http://127.0.0.1:8800/v1 --no-vision --max-steps 6 --no-memory
---
duck: 1
name: e215-hold-on
description: "Hold on to what the jaws hold, flown by a stand-in that never says which way they go."
author: rok
requires: [report_state]
verbs:
  allow: [report_state, gripper, stop]
  confirm: []
budgets:
  max_steps: 6
  max_minutes: 3
  max_llm_calls: 8
success:
  - "You have done what the task asks, as best you can tell from your joints and any camera pictures, or said clearly why you could not."
persona: "Practical and honest: say so when you cannot do something."
---

# Task

Hold on to what the jaws hold. Do not open them.
